[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-19338"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/816c4ecbfe49321bc6b2bc0d72eb61d6ddd1aeae7e76a275df0975439dde5865.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=a+\\lambda b,$ find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=a+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/6782f2fa59056afd9022edbaf69c44a991bf12a7ac6a190bea3cc08fc7a4996c.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=2.5|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.5b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =a+2.5b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=a+\\lambda b=a+2.5b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $b,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =2.5\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-327049/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "91e879d6-45f0-55a9-a966-627d6a5a481b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327049/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "57a5bc70-f8a6-537e-beb8-e1db288ff4ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327049/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "456f1dcc-ef20-59d2-a8c8-6997a0ea7edc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327049/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-327049/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-327049/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327049" :question/id #uuid "6784d6a1-7329-59ce-9957-b8288b4233b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-327049" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/a43139fc26d5778c40db020a7ebc9122c2fd54c0dcd4eb44cfd1671936a4055a.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=\\lambda a+2b,$ then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/1d266a8324d18191f5bc8560be6539d54d1a11916f33ead7432d9f528769fc22.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $2b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=\\frac{1}{2}|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =2b+\\frac{1}{2}a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+2b=\\frac{1}{2}a+2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327049/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fbb8f19-f35a-59c4-9b77-8f6c3542ef28"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327049"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70149/